<p><strong>The design of class discussion or exercise, practice, experience and so on:</strong></p>
<p><strong>Theory teaching</strong></p>
<p><strong><em>1. Female Reproductive Physiology</em></strong></p>
<p>1. To master the structure and function of the organs of the female reproductive system.</p>
<p>2. To master the steps of oogenesis.</p>
<p>3. Differentiate among the phases of the ovarian cycle.</p>
<p>4 master the process of the uterine (menstrual) cycle.</p>
<p>5. aster the functions of progesterone and estrogen.</p>
<p>6. master the e hormonal regulation of the female reproductive cycle (H-P-O axis).</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><em>2. Pregnancy Physiology</em></strong></p>
<p>1. To master the development of embryo and fetal.</p>
<p>2. To master the function of attachment of the fetal.</p>
<p>3. To master maternal changes during pregnancy.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><em>3. Pregnancy & Prenatal Diagnosis</em></strong></p>
<p>3.1 Pregnancy Diagnosis</p>
<p>1. To master common symptom, sign and examination of early pregnancy.</p>
<p>2. To be familiar with common symptom, sign and examination of middle and late pregnancy, and also the definition of fetal lie, fetal presentation and fetal position.</p>
<p>3. To Know differential diagnosis of pregnancy.</p>
<p>3.2 Prenatal Diagnosis</p>
<p>1. To Master common techniques of prenatal diagnosis and Down syndrome screening strategy.</p>
<p>2. To be familiar with the definition and goal of prenatal diagnosis, and neural defects screening strategy.</p>
<p>3. To Know genetic disorders diagnosis strategies and preimplantation diagnosis.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><em>4. Normal Delivery</em></strong></p>
<p>1. To Master the clinical course and management of delivery.</p>
<p>2. To Master the mechanism of labor in occiput presentation.</p>
<p>3. To be familiar with the 4 factors deciding labor and delivery.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><em>5. Ectopic Pregnancy and Abortion</em></strong></p>
<p><strong>5.1 Ectopic Pregnancy</strong></p>
<p>1. To master the definition of ectopic pregnancy.</p>
<p>2. To master the diagnostic process of tubal pregnancy.</p>
<p>3. To master the principles of treatment for tubal pregnancy.</p>
<p>4. To understand the risk factors causing ectopic pregnancy.</p>
<p>5. Some basic concepts. What do STD, ART, hCG, TVS and A-S reaction stand for</p>
<p><strong>5.2 Abortion</strong></p>
<p>1. To master the definition and types of abortion.</p>
<p>2. To master the differential diagnosis of abortion.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><em>6. Abnormal Delivery</em></strong></p>
<p>1. To Master the presentation and diagnosis of abnormalities of expulsive force, birth canal and fetal position.</p>
<p>2. To Master the principle of management for dystocia.</p>
<p>3. To Master the complications of dystocia.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><em>7. Preterm Labor and Premature Rupture of Fetal Membranes</em></strong></p>
<p>1. To Master the definition and causes of preterm labor.</p>
<p>2. To Master the diagnosis and to learn about the treatment of preterm labor.</p>
<p>3. To Master the definition and causes of premature rupture of membranes (PROM).</p>
<p>4. To Master the diagnosis and to learn about the treatment of PROM.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><em>8. Multiple Pregnancy and Disorders of Amnionic Fluid Volume</em></strong></p>
<p><strong>8.1. Multiple Pregnancy</strong></p>
<p>1. To be familiar with what does the multiple pregnancy mean to mother and fetus, risk and complications.</p>
<p>2. To Master the methods of determination between monozygotic and dizygotic.</p>
<p>3. To Master the mechanism and diagnosis of TTTS.</p>
<p><strong>8.2 Disorders of Amnionic Fluid Volume</strong></p>
<p>1. To Master the role of amnionic fluid and its circulation.</p>
<p>2. To be familiar with the methods to evaluate volume of amnionic fluid.</p>
<p>3. To be familiar with what is polyhydramnios or oligohydramnios, the associated conditions, diagnosis, and complications respectively.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><em>9. Bleeding in Late Pregnancy （placenta previa & placenta abruption）</em></strong></p>
<p>1. To master the definition of placenta previa & placenta abruption</p>
<p>2. To master the classification of placenta previa & placenta abruption</p>
<p>3. To master the clinical management of placenta previa & placenta abruption</p>
<p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p>
<p><strong><em>10. Gestational Diabetes Mellitus</em></strong></p>
<p>1. To master screening practices and diagnostic criteria of GDM and PGDM.</p>
<p>2. To master the maternal and fetal complications of GDM.</p>
<p>3. To master diagnosis and treatment of GDM.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><em>11. Postpartum Hemorrhage and Amniotic Fluid Embolism</em></strong></p>
<p><strong>11.1 Postpartum Hemorrhage</strong></p>
<p>1. To be familiar with the causes of postpartum hemorrhage.</p>
<p>2. To Master the procedure to evaluate and treat the postpartum hemorrhage .</p>
<p>3. To be familiar with the prevention of postpartum hemorrhage.</p>
<p><strong>11.2 Amniotic Fluid Embolism</strong></p>
<p>1. To know the risk factors of amniotic fluid embolism</p>
<p>2. To be familiar with the symptoms of amniotic fluid embolism</p>
<p>3. To master the treatment of amniotic fluid embolism</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><em>12. Hypertension in Pregnancy & Intrahepatic Cholestasis Pregnancy</em></strong></p>
<p><strong>12.1 Hypertension in Pregnancy</strong></p>
<p>1. To master hypertension of pregnancy of classification and definitions.</p>
<p>2. To master hypertension of pregnancy of pathology.</p>
<p>3. To master evaluation and management of preeclampsia.</p>
<p><strong>12.2 Intrahepatic Cholestasis Pregnancy</strong></p>
<p>1. To master the clinical manifestation of ICP.</p>
<p>2. To master the diagnosis and differential diagnosis of ICP.</p>
<p>3. To master the management of ICP.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><em>13. Anatomic Disorders of the Female Reproductive System</em></strong></p>
<p>1. To know the development of the female reproductive system.</p>
<p>2. To be familiar with the manifestation, diagnosis and treatment of common anatomic disorders of the female reproductive system.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><em>14. Gynecologic Infection</em></strong></p>
<p>1. To master the definition of cervicitis,&nbsp;vaginitis,&nbsp;vulvitis,&nbsp;and PID</p>
<p>2. To master the clinical signs, diagnosis and principle of treatment.</p>
<p>3. To understand the complications of PID.</p>
<p>4. To master differential diagnosis between female inflammation and tumor.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><em>15. Abnornormal uterine bleeding with ovulatory dysfunction</em></strong></p>
<p>1. To be familiar with the definition and PALM-COEIN classification system of abnormal uterine bleeding (AUB)</p>
<p>2. To understand the etiology and pathophysiological mechanism of AUB with ovulatory dysfunction (AUB-O).</p>
<p>3. To master different pathological changes in endometrium and their clinical significance.</p>
<p>4. To be familiar with the clinical manifestations of AUB-O.</p>
<p>5. To master diagnosis, differential diagnosis and treatment strategy of AUB-O.</p>
<p>6. To be familiar with medication regimen for AUB-O.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><em>16. Amenorrhea</em></strong></p>
<p>1. To know H-P-O axis and the establishment of menstruation</p>
<p>2. To master the primary cause of amenorrhea</p>
<p>3. To master diagnosis of amenorrhea</p>
<p>4. To be familiar with the treatment principles of amenorrhea</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><em>17. Polycystic Ovarian Syndrome</em></strong></p>
<p>1. To know the causes of PCOS.</p>
<p>2. To master the definition and diagnosis of PCOS.</p>
<p>3. To master the treatment methods of PCOS.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><em>18. Cervical Cancer</em></strong></p>
<p>1. To be familiar with the etiology and tumor genesis of cervical cancer.</p>
<p>2. To be familiar with the prognosis, prevention and follow up of cervical cancer.</p>
<p>3.To master the clinical stage and spread of cervical cancer.</p>
<p>4. To master the diagnosis and differential diagnosis of cervical cancer.</p>
<p>5. To master examination and treatment of cervical cancer.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><em>19. Uterine leiomyoma and sarcoma</em></strong></p>
<p>1. To master the four type of degenerations，classification and clinical features of uterine Leiomyoma.</p>
<p>2. To master the effect of myoma on pregnancy.</p>
<p>3. To master the principle and indications of medication treatment and surgery.</p>
<p>4. To be familiar with the causes and diagnosis of uterine leiomyoma.</p>
<p>5. To be familiar with the surgery procedures for myoma.</p>
<p>6. To be familiar with classification of uterine sarcoma and clinical features, diagnosis and prognosis of three common types of uterine sarcoma.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><em>20. Gestational Trophoblastic Disease (GTD)</em></strong></p>
<p>1. To master the definition of GTD and gestational trophoblastic neoplasia (GTN) and to know the differences between the two.</p>
<p>2. To master the symptoms, diagnosis, treatment and follow-up protocol for hydatidiform mole, invasive mole and choriocarcinoma.</p>
<p>3. To know the pathological features of hydatidiform mole, invasive mole and choriocarcinoma.</p>
<p>4. To know the clinical significance of human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG) in GTD.</p>
<p>5. To know the indications of methotrexate (MTX)-based chemotherapy for patients with choriocarcinoma.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><em>21. Endometrial Cancer</em></strong></p>
<p>1. To understand the screening practices and diagnostic criteria of cancer of the endometrium.</p>
<p>2. To understand the the histological classification of endometrial cancer.</p>
<p>3. To master the clinical signs, diagnosis and principle of treatment.</p>
<p>4. To master the differential diagnosis between benign and malignant ovarian tumor.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><em>22. Cervical Intraepithelial Neoplasia and Vulvar Cancer</em></strong></p>
<p><strong>22.1 Vulvar Cancer</strong></p>
<p>1. To master the principle of treatment of vulvar cancer.</p>
<p>2. To know how to prevent the occurrence of vulvar caner.</p>
<p>3. To know how to make a diagnosis of vulvar cancer promptly and correctly.</p>
<p><strong>22.2 Cervical Intraepithelial Neoplasia</strong></p>
<p>1. To be familiar with the definition and risk factors of CIN.</p>
<p>2. To master the diagnostic procedure for CIN and early stage of cervical cancer.</p>
<p>3. To master the classification of CIN and SIL, familiar with the basic rule of treatment of CIN.</p>
<p>4. To know the exact meanings of the following abbreviations: LSIL, HSIL, AIS, CIS and CIN</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><em>23. Endometriosis and adenomyosis</em></strong></p>
<p>At the end of the 2-class hour course, participants should have a good understanding of:</p>
<p>1. The definition, signs and symptoms of endometriosis</p>
<p>2. Different phenotypes of endometriosis</p>
<p>3. The ASRM staging of endometriosis.</p>
<p>4. Multi-disciplinary approach for management of severe endometriosis</p>
<p>5. The definition and imaging features of adenomyosis</p>
<p>6. Principles of treatment for adenomyosis.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><em>24. Ovarian Tumor</em></strong></p>
<p>1. To be familiar with the histological classification of ovarian tumor.</p>
<p>2. To be familiar with the complications of ovarian tumor.</p>
<p>3. To Master the clinical signs, diagnosis and principle of treatment.</p>
<p>4. To Master differential diagnosis between benign and malignant ovarian tumor.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><em>25. Pelvic floor dysfunction</em></strong></p>
<p>1. To master the definition of pelvic organ prolapse&nbsp;(POP),</p>
<p>2. To be familiar with the manifestation, the POP quantification and staging system of pelvic organ prolapse.</p>
<p>2. To be familiar with the definition, etiology and diagnosis of pelvic organ prolapse.</p>
<p>3.To master the definition of stress urinary incontinence.</p>
<p>4. To be familiar with the physical examination and tests of stress urinary incontinence.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><em>26. Infertility</em></strong></p>
<p>1. To be familiar with the frequently used assisted reproductive technology.</p>
<p>2. To be familiar with the complications of assisted reproductive technology.</p>
<p>3. To Master the causes, diagnosis and treatment of infertility.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><em>27. Family planning</em></strong></p>
<p>1. To know the mechanism of hormonal contraception</p>
<p>2. To be familiar with the type of non-hormonal methods of contraception，especially IUD</p>
<p>3. To understand the contraindications of hormonal contraception</p>
<p>4. To understand the methods of early pregnancy termination.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Practice Course Schedule</p>
